\" alt=\"A starfield has a bright pink swirling nebula  in it. The top part of the nebula shows much detail, while the bottom part is mostly open.\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=2560&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2048w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=240&amp;h=300&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 240w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=768&amp;h=960&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=819&amp;h=1024&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 819w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=1229&amp;h=1536&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1229w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=1638&amp;h=2048&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1638w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=320&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 320w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=480&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 480w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=720&amp;h=900&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 720w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=960&amp;h=1200&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 960w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/Shrimp_Pawel_2048.jpg?w=1600&amp;h=2000&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1600w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2048px) 100vw, 2048px\" \/><\/a><\/figure><\/div><\/div><\/div>\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h1 class=\"display-48 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3\">Sh2-188: The Shrimp Nebula<\/h1>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row media-detail-hero__content-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-0 media-detail-hero__description\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Explanation: <\/strong>What causes the swirl in the Shrimp Nebula? Its high speed is likely. What is sure is that <a href=\"https:\/\/ui.adsabs.harvard.edu\/abs\/2005MmSAI..76..477W\/abstract\" rel=\"noopener\">Sh2-188<\/a> is one of the larger <a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/apod\/ap260604.html\" rel=\"noopener\">planetary nebulas<\/a> on the night sky, by <a href=\"https:\/\/www.desmos.com\/calculator\/nkroo5ur9f\" rel=\"noopener\">angular size<\/a>, spanning about half the <a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/apod\/ap251110.html\" rel=\"noopener\">diameter of the Moon<\/a>. Moreover, the <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/asset\/hubble\/signature-of-a-white-dwarf\/\">white-dwarf<\/a> core &#8212; leftover from the <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/sun\/\">Sun<\/a>-like star that shed its outer atmosphere &#8212; is moving unusually fast through interstellar space, creating a <a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/apod\/ap240104.html\" rel=\"noopener\">bow shock<\/a> most visible on the upper left that is <a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/1wqd_RSEhHo\" rel=\"noopener\">similar to<\/a> a boat plowing <a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/95sQcSulRFM?t=3\" rel=\"noopener\">through water<\/a>. Although faint, the <a href=\"https:\/\/app.astrobin.com\/i\/gr8l0a\" rel=\"noopener\">Shrimp Nebula<\/a> glows also by <a href=\"https:\/\/i.imgur.com\/YceJ86e.jpeg\" rel=\"noopener\">compressing<\/a> and brightening gas on its leading edge. The <a href=\"https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/p\/DdBHWd3taKM\/\" rel=\"noopener\">featured image<\/a> was taken in the light of <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Hydrogen-alpha\" rel=\"noopener\">hydrogen<\/a>, sulfur, and oxygen by a backyard telescope in <a href=\"https:\/\/youtu.be\/2CHS7fdbX6o\" rel=\"noopener\">Krakow<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Poland\" rel=\"noopener\">Poland<\/a> and then digitally adjusted to approximate <a href=\"https:\/\/app.astrobin.com\/i\/20aalv\" rel=\"noopener\">the nebula<\/a>&#8216;s true colors.<br><br><strong>APOD&#8217;s email for image submissions has changed.<\/strong> Please see: <a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/apod\/lib\/apsubmit2015.html\" rel=\"noopener\">APOD Submissions<\/a><br><strong>APOD&#8217;s main NASA site has <a href=\"https:\/\/asterisk.apod.com\/viewtopic.php?t=45023\" rel=\"noopener\">moved<\/a>:<\/strong> From <a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/\" rel=\"noopener\">apod.nasa.gov<\/a> to <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/apod\">science.nasa.gov\/apod<\/a><br><strong>Tomorrow&#8217;s picture: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/apod\/fap\/ap260930.html\" rel=\"noopener\">open space<\/a>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"display-none desktop:display-block desktop:grid-col-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-5 margin-top-3 desktop:margin-top-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<table class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-table width-full\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Date<\/th>\n\t\t\