0\" src=\"https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=960&amp;h=640&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"smd-image-rollover__image smd-image-rollover__image--primary\" alt=\"A single color covers the image: that similar to a latte cup of coffee. It is noted in text that apod.nasa.gov is moving to science.nasa.gov\/apod.\" srcset=\"https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=960&amp;h=640&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 960w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=300&amp;h=200&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=768&amp;h=512&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=400&amp;h=267&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=600&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/2026\/september\/CosmicLatte_jhu_960_annotated.jpg?w=900&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" \/><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"960\" height=\"640\" src=\"https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=960&amp;h=640&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"smd-image-rollover__image smd-image-rollover__image--secondary\" alt=\"A single color covers the image: that similar to a latte cup of coffee.\" srcset=\"https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=960&amp;h=640&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 960w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=300&amp;h=200&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=768&amp;h=512&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=400&amp;h=267&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=600&amp;h=400&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https:\/\/assets.science.nasa.gov\/dynamicimage\/assets\/science\/cds\/apod\/apod\/image\/2012\/cosmiclatte_jhu_960.jpg?w=900&amp;h=600&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\" \/><div class=\"toggle-button-container padding-1\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"toggle-view-before-button margin-right-1px is-active\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><span class=\"toggle-view-before-label\">Annotated<\/span><\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"toggle-view-after-button margin-left-1px\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><span class=\"toggle-view-after-label\">Original<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h1 class=\"display-48 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3\">Cosmic Latte: The Average Color of the Universe<\/h1>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row media-detail-hero__content-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-0 media-detail-hero__description\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Explanation:<\/strong> What color is the universe? More precisely, if the <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/image-article\/apod-2002-march-10-a-southern-sky-view\/\">entire sky<\/a> were smeared out, what color would the final mix be? This whimsical <a href=\"http:\/\/sten.astronomycafe.net\/faqs\/\" rel=\"noopener\">question<\/a> came up when trying to determine what stars are commonplace in nearby galaxies. The answer, depicted here, is a <a href=\"https:\/\/www.aao.org\/eye-health\/tips-prevention\/how-humans-see-in-color\" rel=\"noopener\">conditionally perceived shade<\/a> of <a href=\"http:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Beige\" rel=\"noopener\">beige<\/a>. In computer parlance: #<a href=\"https:\/\/www.color-hex.com\/color\/fff8e7\" rel=\"noopener\">FFF8E7<\/a>. To determine this, astronomers computationally averaged the light emitted by one of the larger samples of <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/image-article\/apod-2026-april-23-large-scale-structure-of-the-universe\/\">galaxies<\/a> analyzed: the 200,000 <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/image-article\/apod-2001-september-4-2df-sees-waves-of-galaxies\/\">galaxies<\/a> of the <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/2dF_Galaxy_Redshift_Survey\" rel=\"noopener\">2dF Galaxy Redshift Survey<\/a>. The resulting <a href=\"https:\/\/ui.adsabs.harvard.edu\/abs\/2002ApJ...569..582B\/abstract\" rel=\"noopener\">cosmic spectrum<\/a> has some emission in all parts of the <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/ems\/01_intro\">electromagnetic spectrum<\/a>, but a single perceived composite color. <a href=\"https:\/\/www.curiositybox.com\/blogs\/inqs-corner\/cosmic-latte-the-average-color-of-the-universe\" rel=\"noopener\">This color<\/a> has become much less blue over <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/image-article\/apod-2025-november-23-the-observable-universe\/\">the past<\/a> 10 billion years, indicating that redder stars are becoming <a href=\"https:\/\/www.reddit.com\/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fi.redd.it%2Fprm50mltnj4d1.jpeg\" rel=\"noopener\">more prevalent<\/a>. In a <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Cosmic_latte#Naming_the_color\" rel=\"noopener\">contest<\/a> to better name the color, notable entries included skyvory, univeige, and the winner: <a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Cosmic_latte\" rel=\"noopener\">cosmic latte<\/a>.<br><br><strong>APOD&#8217;s email for image submissions has changed.<\/strong> Please see: <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/apod\/submit\/\">APOD Submissions<\/a><br><strong><em>Tomorrow: <\/em>APOD&#8217;s main NASA site is <a href=\"https:\/\/asterisk.apod.com\/viewtopic.php?t=45023\" rel=\"noopener\">moving<\/a>:<\/strong> From <a href=\"https:\/\/apod.nasa.gov\/\" rel=\"noopener\">apod.nasa.gov<\/a> to <a href=\"https:\/\/science.nasa.gov\/apod\">science.nasa.gov\/apod<\/a><br><strong>Tomorrow&#8217;s picture: <\/strong>sky swirl\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/p>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"display-none desktop:display-block desktop:grid-col-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-5 margin-top-3 desktop:margin-top-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<table class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-table width-full\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Date:<\/th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSeptember 28, 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Color Credit:<\/th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Karl_Glazebrook\" rel=\"noopener\">Karl Glazebrook<\/a> &amp; <a href=\"h